# V3 Color System Usage (`memento-web`)

Use V3 semantic tokens from `docs/COLOR_INVENTORY.md` for all new UI work. Prefer semantic classes (`text-*`, `bg-*`, `border-*`, `fill-*`, `icon-*`) over hex colors or legacy variables.

If the task is broader UI/page construction rather than a tiny token fix, prefer the global `shadcn` skill for choosing/composing existing UI primitives, the global `frontend-design` skill for the overall interface, and the global `emil-design-eng` skill for final polish and taste. This rule still governs the color/token layer.

## Core neutral tokens (default UI)

- `text-neutral-strong`: primary headings, body text, form labels, high-emphasis copy.
- `text-neutral-weak`: secondary text, descriptions, helper text.
- `text-neutral-weaker`: metadata, timestamps, tertiary labels.
- `text-neutral-disabled`: disabled text only.
- `border-neutral-weak` / `stroke-neutral-weak`: input borders, card borders, separators, table dividers.
- `border-neutral-strong` / `stroke-neutral-strong`: active/focused borders and emphasized separators.
- `bg-neutral`: page backgrounds and white surfaces.
- `bg-neutral-weak` / `fill-neutral-weak`: subtle containers, hover rows, quiet sections.
- `bg-neutral-weaker` / `fill-neutral-weaker`: very low-emphasis backgrounds and striped rows.
- `bg-neutral-strong` / `fill-neutral-strong`: dark chips, inverse surfaces, overlays.
- `icon-neutral-strong|weak|weaker|disabled`: icon emphasis ladder matching adjacent text hierarchy.

## Intent token families (status + brand)

- **Brand (`*-brand-*`)**: primary CTA, brand links, selected brand accents.
- **Info (`*-info-*`)**: informational banners, hint states, neutral notifications.
- **Success (`*-success-*`)**: success messages, confirmations, positive badges.
- **Warning (`*-warning-*`)**: cautionary callouts, warning labels.
- **Error (`*-error-*`)**: validation errors, destructive states, danger messaging.

Apply by property type:
- Text color -> `text-{intent}-{strength}`
- Border/ring/stroke -> `border-{intent}-{strength}` or `stroke-{intent}-{strength}`
- Icon color -> `icon-{intent}-{strength}`
- Solid/subtle fill -> `fill-{intent}-{strength}` or `bg-{intent}-{strength}`

Strength semantics:
- `strong`: primary emphasis/action
- `weak`: secondary emphasis
- `weaker`: tertiary/subtle emphasis
- `disabled`: disabled/non-interactive states

## Overlay and modal usage

- `bg-overlay-backdrop`: modal/drawer backdrop in light mode.
- `bg-overlay-backdrop-dark`: modal/drawer backdrop in dark mode.

## Primitive token policy

- Primitive tokens (`--brown-*`, `--neutral-*`, `--orange-*`, `--red-*`, `--amber-*`, `--green-*`, `--blue-*`, `--purple-*`) are source-of-truth implementation tokens.
- In component code, prefer semantic tokens; only use primitives when defining or adjusting token foundations/themes.

## Legacy variable and hex policy

- Do not introduce new hardcoded hex values in app UI.
- Allowed exceptions: SVG/illustration assets, unavoidable third-party overrides, one-off decorative assets explicitly approved.
- Prefer these replacements:
  - `--color-grey-*`, `--color-gray-*` -> nearest `text-neutral-*`, `border-neutral-*`, `bg-neutral-*`, or `fill-neutral-*`
  - onboarding custom colors -> V3 neutral/brand/status equivalents unless intentionally preserving branded onboarding art direction
  - `--overlay-backdrop` / `--overlay-backdrop-dark` -> `bg-overlay-backdrop` / `bg-overlay-backdrop-dark`

## Shadcn + Tailwind implementation guidance

- Use tokenized Tailwind utilities in JSX (`text-neutral-strong`, `border-neutral-weak`, `bg-brand-strong`).
- Keep component color decisions semantic-first: choose intent + strength before choosing a class.
- For states, maintain progression: default `weak/weaker` -> hover `weak/strong` -> active/focus `strong`.
